#140
"Temple of Algesa - Altar Room"
"This temple of Algesa honors the goddess of Law, but in small alcoves along

the temple walls are depictions of the other gods of the realm.  Crowning the

room to the north is an altar of cream-colored marble, with rich gold veins

running through it.  The floor is a polished marble in a darker shade of

cream, and covered with benches of polished ironoak neatly aligned to face the

altar.  The light for the temple is provided by hanging chandeliers with

golden glowing orbs of light, with gold mirrors reflecting and amplifying the

brightness throughout the area.

"
