"wooden shipping crates tops splintered heap corner"
"The crates are old and from the dents and dings in the wood it appears they've

seen a lot of use over the years.  The lids look like they were pried off

hastily and thrown aside, and the straw that once protected the crates'

contents has been scattered all over the floor.  There doesn't appear to be

anything salvageable left in the crates, or anywhere else for that matter.

"
E
"few empty canvas bags floor mold mildew"
"Lying empty, the rough canvas has mildewed into wrinkled stiffness.  A bit of

mold dots the bags here and there, evidence of the leaky roof above.  The bags

that haven't been eaten through with decay appear worthless.

"
E
"rickety table crumpled water-stained papers"
