"wall plain stone"
"Grey river rock has been stacked and mortared to form a thick, rough wall that

runs alongside this abandoned building.  Some of the smaller rocks have broken

off, leaving crumbling indentations that look like handholds of some sort.

The wall rises from the street to about three feet above the rooftop upon

which you stand.  You could probably use the wall to lower yourself to Manor

Road.

"
