#173
"Entrance Hall to a Fortified Manor"
"The entrance hall stretches the length between the building's ornate exit in

the north wall and the even more ornate entryway set in the south wall.  Tall

marble columns carved with ornate figures line the length of the eastern and

western walls on either side of the hall.  Between the center columns an

opening is set in the west and east walls.  Between each of the rest of the

columns is set a tapestry rich with colors depicting some scene of Knightly

prowess.  Overhead a vaulted ceiling is supported by arches extending from

arch to arch in a criss-cross pattern.  Underfoot is a cold floor of carefully

laid cobblestones.

"
"[Joullian] Why is this room a bank?

"
