scrollwork around base and cap.  The arch itself is cut from a single stone

and bears a caption on the side reading: Honor, Law, Protection, and Unity

"
E
"1 south entryway"
"The ornate arch is formed of a sculpted knight in full armor on either side

with swords raised and crossed to form the lintel overhead.  The arch is

carved from pristine white marble and shines with a glossy finish.

"
E
"tapestry tapestries"
"The tapestries are relatively new with brightly colored greens, reds, blues

and the like forming its woven images.  Each of the half dozen tapestries

depict a great scene of Knightly valor.  Four depict great scenes of battle

being lain to rest by the strength of the Knights who impose peace after such

actions.  The remaining four tapestries show a different Knight defeating a

hydra, a basilisk, a manticore and even a dragon in single combat.  No names

are given to define who these Knights are allowing all to share equally in

their glory.

"
E
"1 down floor 6 cobblestones"
"The cobblestones are so well placed that not even a knife can be placed

between them forming a fairly smooth floor.

