#181
"Base of the Ivory Tower"
"The broad circular base of the tower forms one large singular room.  Its walls

are lined with tapestries of heroic deeds being completed by a wide variety of

adventurers long past.  A warm fireplace is set in the northernmost arc of the

wall.  A marble bench sits before it providing a place of repose.  Starting on

the easternmost arc of the wall and spiraling up the wall in a counter-

clockwise fashion is a grand staircase marked by ornate stonework at every

riser.

