"3 trophies trophy"
"The trophies are the results of many heros' quests donated for these walls.

They represent any number of strange and wonderful results including such

things as beasts slain in mortal combat and less brutal but no less honorable

rewards such as beautiful instruments and objects such as sparkling grails and

glimmering magical mirrors earned in reward for tasks completed.  Largest and

fiercest among the trophies is a large dragon's head mounted over the mantle

of the fireplace.

"
E
"dragon head"
"The head is covered in thick scales of a scarlet red tinged with the slightest

touches of grey at the fringes that encroached upon the scales with extreme

age.  Its ivory teeth, though ancient, retain the serrated sharpness of keen

knives and look able to chew their way through the toughest plate armor.  Some

artist has even managed to set a pair of lifelike eyes with a most baleful

glare in the sockets where the dragon's real eyes once resided.  The entire

effect remains awe-inspiring and frightful even in the stillness of death.

"
E
"3 grails"
"Ornate chalices of silver and gold often covered in sparkling gems in a

multitude of colors.  Each was given to some hero as a reward for an act of

bravery or as the reward for some perilous undertaking.

"
E
"3 mirrors"
"The mirrors reflect the warm light of the torches around the room enhancing

their glow.  Arcane symbols around the edges of some indicate that they are

probably quite magical in nature though it is unclear how they may be used.

"
E
"1 down 3 stairs"
"The stairs lead down through a hole in the floor near the west wall and head

down into the lower tower in a clockwise manner.  A sturdy banister prevents

anyone from accidently tripping into the hole for the stairwell.

"
E
"1 up 4 overhead 4 ceiling 4 stars 4 treeline"
